Persistent bundles third-party open-source software that remains under its
own license, not under the PolyForm Noncommercial License. The bundled npm
packages are listed, with their license texts, in generated notices files:

- apps/web/public/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt: the web app, which every Persistent
  app also shows. Served at /THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt and linked from Settings.
- apps/linux-desktop/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt: the Linux AppImage's own
  packages, shipped inside the AppImage. Electron's and Chromium's licenses
  ship inside the AppImage as well (LICENSE and LICENSES.chromium.html).

Both are generated by devkit-notices from the x64 production dependencies.
The arm64 AppImage differs only in its native binary packages.

The API server image runs only on the maintainer's server and is not
distributed, so it has no notices file. The Android app generates its own notices
at build time (AboutLibraries, apps/mobile/android-plugin/third-party-notices.gradle)
into the APK, where the app's notices page shows them after the web list. The
Windows app's notices are generated from its NuGet restore graph by winui-app-kit
(apps/desktop/Persistent.Desktop/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt), ship beside the app,
and are linked from its About page.
